-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for Doubling (doc/cross-term.pdf,
-- Section 3: Lemmas 3-6, Corollary 7): one entry per declaration, generated from
-- --opened (28 Oct 2026) and checked against the note by kind.  Kinds:
--   types and levels: PtMap, PtSec, PtEquiv, Maps.PMO, PiOne.O, isTrunc, isConn,
--     isProp, isSet, NatArith.plus (index arithmetic);
--   by-definition steps of the text: LoopConj.conj (conj p u = p^-1 . u . p),
--     KMap.conj (conj_m F = e ; F ; e^-1), KMap.K / map0 / c0 at m = 0, zeroH,
--     twoH, xor, Z2ab (Lemma 2), sq, ptcomp, ptconst, trans and ap (ap-diag,
--     loop-sq), EH.O / EH.comp (whiskerings), PiOne.comp / Induced.L (L-def,
--     comp-def), SqConj.G (G-def), Pmo.Stmt, Dbl.Stmt, KK.e / EMSpace.loops and
--     pt-inv / Acc.inv in Dbl.Step.h (e_{m+1} and its inverse, by definition);
--   extras, not steps of the text:
--     Dbl.h0 opens the implementation of the band (EM1.unband, TrivG.emb, img,
--       kb-be) when band-unband / band-hom are checked; the same checker-defect
--       candidate as Presentation.Rec.cell1 (present.opens);
--     Dbl.h0' opens KK.K, KK.pt, EMSpace.K, EMSpace.pt to identify K(A,1) with
--       EM1.K1 (KK.K 1 = EMSpace.K 0 = EM1.K1 by definition), because c0 is
--       stated on EM1.K1 and PMO_0 on KK.K 1.
